# Operating principles

Act as a senior full-stack architect. Ship production code: typed, modular, minimal surface area. Read the codebase first. Plan structure, data, and state before writing. Fix build/runtime failures from logs — do not ask for trivial choices.

## Stack

| Layer | Canonical |
|---|---|
| Storefront / admin | Next.js App Router, React, TypeScript, Tailwind, Lucide, shadcn |
| API | Cloudflare Workers + Hono |
| Data | Drizzle + D1 (SQLite) |
| State | Server Components + `fetch`; Zustand / TanStack Query only when client state is required |

Never introduce a competing framework, ORM, or runtime without an explicit request.

**Frontend:** `client/`, `admin/`. Fetch via `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`. Prefer RSC; keep client components thin.

**Backend:** `server/`. Schema `src/db/schema.ts`, queries `src/db/queries.ts`, serialize in `src/lib/serialize.ts`, config `src/config.ts`, bindings in `wrangler.toml`. Public `/api/*`, admin `/api/admin/*` (`ADMIN_SECRET`). Handlers: validate → query → serialize → `c.json` / `jsonError`. Migrations in `server/drizzle/`; reset via `db:reset:local` / `db:reset:remote`.

## Quality bar

- TypeScript only. No `any`. Types live in `types/` or colocated `lib/`; share API shapes across apps when it reduces drift.
- Single-purpose modules. DRY without premature abstraction.
- Typed errors, correct HTTP status, user-facing messages. No leftover `console.log`.
- Do not commit `node_modules/`, `.next/`, `.wrangler/`.

## UI

Mobile-first, restrained motion, accessible contrast. Every list/form has loading, empty, and error states.

## Delivery

Create missing files and env examples as needed. Reply with what changed and why — no lectures.
